WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:07.290
Let's get back to hearing from you via discord
at David Pakman dotcom slash discord.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.900
Let's go next to Adam from Los Angeles, California.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.330
Adam, you're on the air.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.349
Hey, David.

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:18.320
So I actually wanted to ask about DACA and
the Dreamers.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.500
Obviously, it's been a roller coaster for
them.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.410
And, you know, now with a slim majority in
the House and Senate, how likely do you think

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:34.730
it'll be for not only people who are in DACA,
but people who maybe narrowly do not qualify

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.860
to get some relief?

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:41.910
I'm confident that the current DACA participants,
current participant doesn't seem like the

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.829
right word, those who currently qualify for
DACA status.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:50.860
I think that in relatively short order, they
are going to be taken care of now in terms

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.489
of expanding DACA to include more people.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:56.820
I think there's more of a question mark around
that, and it's really too early for me to

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.870
have a strong sense of of how likely it is
that DACA will be expanded.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:08.030
Totally, yeah, because I know even as recently
as twenty nineteen, the DREAM Act obviously

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.409
got blocked by Mitch McConnell in the Senate.

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:11.409
Yeah.

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:13.960
And didn't even be it wasn't even brought
to a vote.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.970
But I know the bill itself has always had
bipartisan support, so hopefully something

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.970
can happen there.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:26.780
You know, the disgusting reality is there
are despite bipartisan support, there are

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:33.880
likely Republicans who may want to stand in
the way merely to deny Joe Biden an accomplishment

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.880
on this.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:38.390
And that's really sad because we're talking
about people's lives being at stake here.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.340
Yeah, livelihood's maybe better said no.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.680
I think it's disgusting.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.830
And I guess the hope is that, you know, something
can get done about that.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:53.080
You know, would they need any bipartisan support
even to pass it to?

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.790
You know, that's a really interesting question.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.490
It's without really reading more about it.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:04.020
I don't know how much can be done by simple
majority, how much can be done by executive

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.920
order and how much would need 60, 60 votes.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.770
And so I don't have an answer on that at this
immediate moment.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.690
I think it's something I'm going to have to
read up on.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:14.690
Absolutely.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:16.980
Well, thank you so much for your time, David.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.980
My pleasure.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:26.750
Great to great to speak with you.

